  "photoModel": {
    "title": "Itaewon 이태원",
    "description": "Itaewon is a bastardized district just east of the former US Eighth Army Headquarters. Having long catered to the US military, it has always had a very foreign feel. Now, with Seoul being home to more and more foreigners of many different nationalities, Itaewon has also attracted a sizable Muslim population, mostly working-class guest workers, due to the presence of Seoul's main mosque.\n\nHere I can see Muslim Fabrics and Madinah Travel. Many businesses do cater to the area's Muslim migrant worker population, and indeed most people out and about on some alleyways are South Asians, quite unexpected in Korea, a country traditionally known for being very monoethnic and not having any significant foreigner/ethnic minority population.",
